# Production Agents

## Invariant

Other modules call **`AiModule` only** — never `module_ai.agents` or `module_ai.services`.
There is no `module-ai` HTTP router. SSE is mounted by `module-chat`.

The graph that runs is the production graph. LangGraph Studio, when it exists, is a local debugger and is not the runtime.

## Agent layout (target)

```
module_ai/agents/
├── base.py
├── investigator/     # v1 graph
├── reporter/         # planned
└── alert_triage/     # planned
```

Do not add a general chatbot graph.

## Facade

`AiModule.investigate` is the v1 entry. Chat prepare stays off the API event loop once streaming exists.

## Tools

- The agent calls our MCP server.
- Tools return aggregates or a small sample (`get_event_samples`).
- v1 tools are read-only, rate-limited, and non-destructive.
- `ack_alert` and `run_safe_sql` are later. SQL is an allowlist, not free-form.

## Dependencies

`module-ai` must not import events, metrics, anomalies, or chat internals.
LLM calls go through `LlmPort`. The first adapter is Ollama.

## Trace

Each run logs `AGENT_START`, each tool name, `CONCLUSION` with evidence, and `AGENT_END` (latency, tools_used, tokens_local).

